	affiliations = {University of British Columbia, Computer Science, Okanagan, Kelowna, Canada},
	abstract = {This paper explores the application of Machine Learning (ML) and Item Response Theory (IRT) to develop an adaptive learning framework for personalized quizzes in programming education. With the increasing demand for computing skills across diverse fields, the proposed system dynamically tailors questions to individual student abilities and learning styles. By continuously evaluating student performance, the system refines question types and difficulty levels to ensure a customized learning experience. Additionally, the system uses a mastery tracking mechanism to monitor student proficiency across topics and categories, enabling targeted learning interventions. To validate this approach, we implemented uLearn, an online e-learning system, and conducted an exploratory study. Results demonstrated improved student performance, enhanced comprehension, increased engagement, and a strong preference to continue using adaptive learning in the future.  © 2025 IEEE.},
