	abstract = {E-learning platforms demand effective question-generation methods, and large language models have made this easier. While recent studies focused on generating questions from text, no prior research has evaluated their ability to generate questions from code. This work presents a framework to evaluate the models in question generation from code using average scores, win rates, and Elo ratings. Python, C++, and Java code were used to prompt models. The evaluation includes automatic metrics and human evaluators. Findings show GPT-4-0314, GPT-4-0613, and GPT-3.5-turbo-0613 outperform others, with GPT-4-0314 leading in score (8.86), win rate (1.000), and Elo rating, 2616. © 2025 The Author(s). Open Access statement. This is an open-access article distributed under the terms of the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/), which permits unrestricted use, distribution, and reproduction in any medium, provided the original author and source are credited, a link to the CC License is provided, and changes – if any – are indicated. (SID_1)},
