	abstract = {To gain deeper insights into the development of computational thinking (CT) among college students in online environments, this study introduces two scaffolding strategies - cloze code hints and pseudo code hints - and investigates their effects on the dynamic trajectories of novice programmers' CT abilities. The results from discourse analysis and cognitive network modeling indicate that both scaffolding strategies significantly enhance the development of CT. Specifically, cloze code hints facilitate novice programmers' transitions between various CT dimensions more effectively. Conversely, pseudo code hints foster iterative optimization behaviors among learners when tackling complex problem-solving tasks. These findings offer valuable insights for the effective cultivation and enhancement of students' computational thinking skills. © 2025 IEEE.},
