	affiliations = {Normal Branch College, Yanbian University, Jilin, Yanji, China},
	abstract = {Aiming at the problems of low learning efficiency, poor knowledge points and lack of real-time feedback in traditional programming teaching, this study designs a personalized programming teaching system based on generative AI. The system adopts a three-layer technical architecture: 1) Construct a fine-grained knowledge graph based on the Transformer code understanding model to realize programming concept dependency modeling, 2) Integrate a dynamic difficulty adjustment algorithm to generate adaptive exercises by real-time analysis of learner code submission features, 3) Deploy a multimodal feedback engine, combine program semantic parsing and natural language generation technology to generate defect location and reconstruction suggestions. The experimental results show that the system significantly improves learning efficiency (the average task time is 38.2 minutes) and knowledge point mastery (92.4%), and the feedback response delay is only 0.9 seconds, providing a feasible solution for intelligent programming education. © 2025 IEEE.},
