	affiliations = {Department of Computer Science, Boston College, Chestnut Hill, 02467, MA, United States},
	abstract = {While adaptive AI tutoring can enhance learning outcomes in fundamental computer science, excessive reliance on AI-generated solutions may reduce cognitive engagement, which is essential for deep understanding. To address this, we introduce the Encouraging and Engaging Assignment Assistant (E<sup>2A2)</sup> an AI-powered tutoring system designed to foster active learning, structured guidance, and academic integrity in introductory programming courses. Unlike conventional AI systems that provide complete solutions, E<sup>2A2</sup> employs step-by-step guidance, retrieval-augmented generation, and adaptive feedback to promote meaningful engagement with learning modules rather than passive answer consumption. By integrating course materials, assignment guidelines, and student progress tracking, E<sup>2A2</sup> delivers context-aware, personalized support that strengthens problem-solving and programming skills. By redefining AI's role from an answer provider to a learning facilitator, E<sup>2A2</sup> offers a scalable, ethical approach to AI-driven tutoring, bridging the gap between AI assistance and authentic student learning. © 2025 IEEE.},
