	affiliations = {College of Digital Media, Chongqing Polytechnic University of Electronic Technology, Chongqing, China; School of Education, Universiti Utara Malaysia, Malaysia; UUM College of Arts and Sciences (Pendidikan), Universiti Utara Malaysia, Malaysia},
	abstract = {Educational institutions are increasingly exploring how teachers' personal qualities and technology use impact student motivation. This study examined whether teachers' pedagogical stewardship sense (a teacher's felt responsibility for guiding student learning) influences students' scholastic motivation, and whether this effect occurs through enhanced collaborative classroom interaction. We further assessed if AI-enhanced teaching integration (the extent to which instructors incorporate AI tools in teaching) moderates this process. Using a three-wave survey design in Chinese programming courses, we collected data at staggered intervals to reduce common method bias. The results indicated that teachers who exhibit a strong sense of pedagogical stewardship foster more collaborative interactions among students, which in turn is associated with higher student motivation. Notably, this indirect relationship was more pronounced when instructors highly integrated AI tools into their teaching. These findings suggest that supportive teacher attitudes coupled with thoughtful AI tool use can create a more interactive learning environment that energizes students' motivation. The study contributes to educational psychology and technology integration research by highlighting how teacher dispositions and AI-facilitated pedagogy jointly shape student engagement and motivation, offering practical insights for enhancing learning in the digital age. © 2025},
