	affiliations = {Zhejiang Normal University, College of Education, Jinhua, China; Zhejiang Normal University, School of Computer Science and Technology, Jinhua, China},
	abstract = {Self-regulated learning (SRL) plays a crucial role in programming education. However, many students struggle to effectively manage their learning processes when solving programming problems. To address this challenge, this study developed CodeBuddy, a conversational educational system powered by large language models (LLMs), designed to provide structured SRL support throughout the programming problem-solving process. Grounded in Zimmerman's SRL theory, the system structures learning into five stages and provides tailored guidance covering metacognitive, cognitive, behavioral, and motivational aspects. Through continuous interaction and personalized feedback, CodeBuddy not only assists students in completing programming tasks, but also promotes the sustained development of their self-regulation skills. In addition, the system records student interactions to support teachers in instructional analysis and formative feedback. This study offers a new practical framework that integrates SRL theory with generative AI technologies, contributing to both learner autonomy and improved learning outcomes in programming education. © 2025 IEEE.},
